  ## Transcript
  
  The public works search contains all the
  MLC's musical works ownership data.
  Anyone can search the MLC's public work
  search using this search window free of
  charge. The accuracy and completeness of
  the MLC's data is determined solely by
  our members, the music publishers,
  administrators, self-administered
  songwriters, composers, and lyricists
  who are entitled to collect mechanical
  royalties from the MLC. Please note, you
  can't edit a work from the public
  search. If the work you are searching
  for exists, click into the work to
  review the current claimments. If you
  need to claim shares in this work,
  please utilize the claiming tool in your
  member portal. Generally, if you have an
  agreement with a publishing
  administration service, the service will
  register your works with the MLC and
  collect your share of royalties on your
  behalf. Please refer to the service to
  which you are assigned directly to
  confirm registration of your shares of
  musical works with the MLC.
  You cannot update information via the
  public search. To edit work details such
  as duration, song ID, ISWC, or adding a
  new writer, publisher, or recording, you
  can edit that information in your work
  catalog by clicking edit next to the
  relevant section. However, if you need
  to edit existing writer or publisher
  information, you will need to contact
  our support team to make those updates
  internally.
  If you are a writer that has someone
  else administering your works, you will
  need to contact your publisher or
  administrator to edit this information.
  If you are unable to register a share of
  a work because another party is already
  claiming all or part of the same share
  resulting in a conflict, then you may
  seek to resolve the conflict through a
  conflict procedure as outlined in the
  ownership dispute policy. Please use the
  contact us form to notify the MLC of a
  potential conflict.
  The public work search is accessible not
  only from our website page in the upper
  right hand corner but also from your
  member portal.
  Using the public work search, you can
  add multiple search criteria such as
  work title, ISWC code, MLC song code,
  writer IPI, publisher name, and
  publisher IPI.
  Using the work title field, I'm going to
  search to see if this work exists within
  our database. I'm also going to use the
  writer name field to enter the writer
  name of this work as well.
  We now see six relevant search results
  based on these search criteria.
  Clicking into the work, I can review
  details
  such as any ISWC codes or work details,
  alternate titles,
  writer name, as well as any writer IPIs
  that have been listed.
  I can also review publishers that are
  currently claimants on this work.
  Additionally, you'll be able to see any
  matched recordings. These are recordings
  that have been matched to this work
  through automation as well as a manual
  matching process.
  The MLC public work search allows anyone
  to review works data within the MLC's
  database.
