  The Office has long rejected the suggestion to place a confidentiality requirement on copyright owners receiving statements of account under the section 115 license due to the inclusion of “competitively sensitive” information (
  _e.g.,_
  licensees' overall revenues, royalty payments to record companies and performance rights organizations, and overall usage). [79 FR 56190](https://www.federalregister.gov/citation/79-FR-56190), [56206](https://www.federalregister.gov/citation/79-FR-56206) (Sept. 18, 2014). Rather, “once the statements of account have been delivered to the copyright owners, there should be no restrictions on the copyright owners' ability to use the statements or disclose their contents.”
  _Id._
  In a recent parallel rulemaking, the Office again declined to adopt confidentiality restrictions on copyright owners receiving statements of account. 85 FR at 22561.
  
  
